    {
      "id": "the-mandubii",
      "year": "52 BC",
      "sortYear": -52,
      "headline": "The Mandubii",
      "body": "The food inside runs out first. Vercingetorix expels the Mandubii — the people whose town it is, the ones not fighting. Women, children and the old walk down to the Roman lines and ask to be let through. Caesar refuses. They cannot go back up and they cannot come forward, so they stay in the open ground between the walls, where both armies can see them, and starve. Caesar records this in one sentence and moves on.",
