    {
      "id": "two-battles",
      "year": "52 BC",
      "sortYear": -52,
      "headline": "Two battles in one day",
      "body": "The relief force arrives and attacks both walls at once. Vercassivellaunus finds the single place the fortifications could not follow the ground — a slope on the northwest where the line runs wrong — and throws sixty thousand men at it. Labienus is sent with what can be spared. Caesar takes cavalry out through his own lines and comes around behind the attackers, in a red cloak, deliberately visible, so that both armies know exactly where he is.",
